    description: "Residual of INV-hamin (PR #1320). ADR-0061 ruling 1 places in-repo catalogue data in .hypergumbo.toml's catalogue keys AND <repo>/.hypergumbo/<family>.d/ (catalogue_home.repo_catalogue_home). The .toml keys now load only on opt-in (--in-repo-catalogues / trust-catalogues). The .d directories are read by nothing, so there is no hazard today -- but a user following the ADR and the registry docstring ('repo tier: <repo>/.hypergumbo/') gets no effect and no error, the io_primitives.d shape WI-talaz closed once. Work: read each wired channel's in-repo directory behind the same opt-in gate, list its files under catalog_provenance tiers.in_repo with git state, and decide per family whether in-repo rows get the yours treatment once opted in (ruling 2 says un-opted in-repo rows only add)."  # 2095
